- Cheapest decisive test: **(b)**—construct the common integral model and certify relative smoothness at one \(B=84\) witness. Formal smoothness then gives the \(p\)-adic lift by the [infinitesimal lifting criterion](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02H6).
- Hardest gate: global chart compatibility plus realization by one polynomial Keller pair.
- [Artin approximation](https://eudml.org/doc/141922) and [Abhyankar–Moh](https://doi.org/10.1515/crll.1975.276.148) do not bridge that gate.
